From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 17:59:40 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 125/125] go.mod: sing-quic from a fork with the input
 validation of UDP packets

Two upstream commits on top of the version this line pins, f693b76 and e702a73
(github.com/FiyeroT/sing-quic), without the rework of the clients that upstream
made between them and the pinned one. A TUIC server could end the process with
a fragmented UDP packet of more than 65535 bytes: the sum of the fragments
overflowed, the buffer came out too small and the write into it panicked. A
datagram size from a Hysteria, Hysteria2 or TUIC server no larger than the
header of a fragment made the split of a packet panic or loop for ever.
---
 go.mod | 2 ++
 go.sum | 4 ++--
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

